      "text": [
        " \"نَعَمْ\" قُلْتُ فَيَهُودِيٌّ أُشْهِدَ عَلَى شَهَادَةٍ ثُمَّ أَسْلَمَ أَ تَجُوزُ شَهَادَتُهُ قَالَ \"نَعَمْ\"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.3354 - Safwan ibn Yahya asked Abu al-Hasan (as):\nAbout a man who made his employee a witness to a testimony and then separated from him, would his testimony be valid after their separation?\nImam (as) said: \"Yes.\"\nHe further asked: What if a Jew was made a witness to a testimony and then embraced Islam, would his testimony be valid?\nImam (as) said: \"Yes.\""
        ]
      }
